      "closure_rationale": "The assessor derives1+2^32+2^64 plus the finite byte-sequence sum. Separate active-member selection, value semantics and release authority are implemented. Actual GCC/Clang default/missing-enumerator controls show diagnostics depend on flags; actual Rust exhaustive/wildcard probes distinguish language checking from a logical default-path omission. Actual retained pair elimination promotes before addition and preserves scalar output on wrong tag. Every old operation has an explicit TEXT migration rule; borrowed source bytes are copied before mutation and a source-policy clone replaces a destination-policy owner only after success. Text length, embedded zero and empty-text-versus-EMPTY are separate states. Six native profiles execute the two actual retained sum mutants plus six owning controls, all normal semantic rejections. Enum-size/runtime and compiler branch/stack/dependency observations are source-bound; fourteen diagnostic observations include before/after positive clients and E0004. Independent10512 histories/56384 transitions compare values and owner counts. Fallible clone/drop callbacks allocate actual storage and inject both preallocation and postallocation-cleanup failure. Old destination survives, including an input suffix borrowing its payload; self-copy/move call no callback, moves empty the source, policy transfer drops the old context once, and repeated drop is harmless. Changed clients that fail diagnostics and clients preserving a default path are both executed. This is author support for the stated finite callback contract, not acceptance of independent learner work."
    },
